* Pwc "## Parameters" claim: points= is sorted ascending by x at parse time, so declaration
* order does not matter -- this list is given newest-point-first and must behave exactly like
* example.cir's STEP (holds 0 until t = 0.001, then 1). Also proves repeat= is matched exactly:
* "True" (Python-style capitalization) is NOT the string "true", so no wrapping happens and the
* value holds flat past the last point (see
* test_pwc.py::test_points_sorted_at_parse_and_repeat_is_exact_true).
A kind=pwc points=[[0.001,1],[0,0]] repeat=True
